<title>UK: World Bank sets 1.0 trillion lire zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank sets 1.0 trillion lire zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Credito Italiano and Citibank International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT    ONE TRLN LIRE COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    07.NOV.16</p>
<p> TYPE   ZERO-COUPON   ISS PRICE  23.144    PAY DATE    07.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0 PCT   REOFFER    21.294    SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50-500  SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  1.85</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF A GLOBAL MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
